# Frontend Standards

## Stack (non-negotiable)

- **Language**: TypeScript (strict)
- **Framework**: Next.js App Router (`app/`)
- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS utility classes; shared tokens via `tailwind.config` / CSS variables
- Call FastAPI over REST (`NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL`); never call Gemini/Pinecone from the browser

## Primary UI: ChatGPT-like interface (required)

Conversational chat layout — not a form dashboard.

### Layout

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  header / brand                         │
├─────────────────────────────────────────┤
│  message thread (scrollable)            │
│  - user bubbles                         │
│  - assistant bubbles + citations        │
├─────────────────────────────────────────┤
│  attachment chips / previews            │
│  [+] composer: textarea + send          │
└─────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

- Full-height chat shell; thread scrolls; composer pinned to bottom
- User right-aligned; assistant left-aligned with RAG citations
- Empty state invites a question or file attach
- Show streaming / pending feedback while waiting on the API

### Composer & attachments (required)

Match **Gemini Embedding 2 Preview** limits (see `embedding-modality-specs`):

| Modality | Accept only | UI behavior / limit |
|----------|-------------|---------------------|
| Text | paste / `.txt` | Cap ~8,192 tokens (~6,000 words); show over-limit error |
| PDF | `.pdf` | Filename + size; long PDFs **auto-split every 6 pages** on the backend |
| Image | `.png`, `.jpg`, `.jpeg` | Thumbnail; max **6 images** per request |
| Audio | `.mp3`, `.wav` | Filename + duration; reject if **> 80s** |
| Video | `.mp4`, `.mov` | Filename + duration; reject if **> 120s** |

- **Upload** is a separate control: selecting/dropping files uploads & indexes immediately via `POST /api/upload`
- **Send** sends the text question only via `POST /api/chat` (no combined file+message submit)
- Show per-file status: Checking → Uploading N% → Indexing → Uploaded / Failed

## Structure

```
frontend/
  app/
    layout.tsx
    page.tsx              # chat shell entry
    globals.css           # Tailwind layers + CSS variables
  components/
    chat/                 # Thread, Bubble, Composer, AttachMenu, CitationList
  lib/
    api.ts                # typed fetch to FastAPI
    attachments.ts        # accept lists, validation, previews
    types.ts              # Message, Citation, Modality
  public/
  tailwind.config.ts
  tsconfig.json
```

## TypeScript & React

- Prefer Server Components by default; mark chat interactivity with `"use client"`
- Typed props and API DTOs; no `any` unless bridging untyped third-party data
- Colocate chat state (messages, attachments, status) in focused client components/hooks

## Tailwind

- Utility-first; extract repeated patterns into components, not giant `@apply` blocks
- Mobile-first breakpoints; composer and attach menu usable on narrow viewports
- Light chrome for bubbles/chips; subtle motion for send/receive and typing indicator

## States

- Empty, loading, upload progress, per-file validation errors, API errors — all explicit
- Assistant replies must show citations (source, modality, id/link when available)
